# The backend image is built from the repo root so pnpm can resolve the
# workspace catalog (see backend/Dockerfile). Without this file the whole
# monorepo — three node_modules trees, the parser's multi-megabyte game
# fixtures, the web build — gets uploaded to the daemon on every build.

# Never useful in an image, and copying a host node_modules into a Linux
# container is how you get native modules built for the wrong platform.
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
.github
.idea
.claude

# Other workspace packages. web deploys via Vercel and parsing runs locally;
# neither belongs in the API image. pnpm-workspace.yaml still lists them, which
# is harmless — the globs simply match nothing.
web/
parsing/
youtube/
docs/

# Local-only backend state: the Mongo data directory bind-mounted by
# docker-compose.yml, and the dev .env (the server injects its own via
# env_file: sf.env, and dotenv does not override real environment variables).
backend/data/
backend/.env

*.md
!README.md
